odifiedTimeUtc\":\"2021-04-13T07:33:33.0348454Z\",\"createdTimeUtc\":\"2021-04-13T07:33:33.0348454Z\",\"incidentNumber\":10444889,\"additionalData\":{\"alertsCount\":1,\"bookmarksCount\":0,\"commentsCount\":0,\"alertProductNames\":[\"Microsoft Cloud App Security\"],\"tactics\":[]},\"relatedAnalyticRuleIds\":[\"/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"],\"incidentUrl\":\"https://portal.azure.com/#asset/Microsoft_Azure_Security_Insights/Incident/subscriptions/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/resourceGroups/sentinel-check/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/Incidents/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"providerName\":\"Azure Sentinel\",\"providerIncidentId\":\"XXXXX\"}}]","DisplayResult":true}],"Parameters":[{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"3","DisplayName":"Time Frame","Description":"Time frame in hours for which to fetch Incidents","OptionalValues":[]},{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"New, Active, Closed","DisplayName":"Status","Description":"Statuses of the incidents to look for. Comma-separated string","OptionalValues":[]},{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"Informational, Low, Medium, High","DisplayName":"Severity","Description":"Severities of the incidents to look for. Comma-separated string.","OptionalValues":[]},{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"200","DisplayName":"How Many Incidents to Fetch","Description":"How many incidents to fetch","OptionalValues":[]}],"AICategories":["Enrichment"],"AIDescription":"### General Description\nThe **List Incidents** action retrieves a list of incidents from Microsoft Azure Sentinel based on specific search criteria. It allows security analysts to query the external system for incidents within a defined time window, filtered by their current status and severity levels. The results are presented as a structured data table and a raw JSON output for further automation steps.\n\n### Parameters Description\n| Parameter | Type | Mandatory | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Time Frame** | Integer | No | The number of hours back from the current time to search for incidents. Defaults to 3 hours if not specified. |\n| **Status** | String | No | A comma-separated list of incident statuses to include (e.g., 'New, Active, Closed'). Defaults to all three. |\n| **Severity** | String | No | A comma-separated list of incident severities to include (e.g., 'Informational, Low, Medium, High'). Defaults to all four. |\n| **How Many Incidents to Fetch** | Integer | No | The maximum number of incident records to retrieve. Defaults to 200. |\n\n### Flow Description\n1. **Initialization**: The action extracts integration configuration (API credentials, workspace details) and user-provided search parameters.\n2. **Validation**: It validates that the provided `Status` and `Severity` strings contain values recognized by the Microsoft Azure Sentinel API.\n3. **Query Construction**: A query is built using the `QueryBuilder` utility to filter incidents by `createdTimeUtc`, `status`, and `severity` using OData filter syntax.\n4. **Data Retrieval**: The action sends a GET request to the Azure Sentinel incidents endpoint.\n5. **Output Generation**: Retrieved incidents are parsed into a standardized data model. The action then populates a data table in the Google SecOps UI and attaches the full incident details as a JSON result.","EntityTypes":[]}